solutionFiles.Program.cs:
// Road trip calculator. Fix it so the output matches the instructions.
string destination = "Grand Canyon";
int distanceKm = 735;
double kmPerLitre = 14.5;
decimal pricePerLitre = 1.62m;
int friends = 4;

double litres = distanceKm / kmPerLitre;
decimal fuelCost = (decimal)litres * pricePerLitre;
decimal perPerson = fuelCost / friends;

Console.WriteLine($"Trip to {destination}");
Console.WriteLine($"Fuel needed: {litres:F1} L");
Console.WriteLine($"Fuel cost: {fuelCost:F2}");
Console.WriteLine($"Each friend pays: {perPerson:F2}");

hints.markdown:
The two calculation lines:

```csharp
double litres = distanceKm / kmPerLitre;
decimal fuelCost = (decimal)litres * pricePerLitre;
```

Then print with `$"Trip to {destination}"`, `{litres:F1}`, `{fuelCost:F2}` and `{perPerson:F2}`.
